<title>USA: Pall Q3 shr loss narrows.</title>
<headline>Pall Q3 shr loss narrows.</headline>
<dateline>EAST HILLS, N.Y. 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>CONSOLIDATED STATEMENTS OF EARNINGS PALL CORPORATION</p>
<p>(Amounts in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>			  THIRD QUARTER ENDED    NINE MONTHS ENDED</p>
<p>			    MAY 3,     APR. 27,   MAY 3,   APR. 27,</p>
<p>				1997	  1996	1997	1996</p>
<p>REVENUES</p>
<p> Net sales	     $275,339    $277,376 $771,889   $762,701</p>
<p>COSTS AND EXPENSES</p>
<p> Cost of sales     139,099(a)     109,696  346,974(a) 307,552</p>
<p>Selling, general and administrative expenses</p>
<p>			     92,190	96,141  282,368    278,270</p>
<p>Research and development</p>
<p>			     13,761	14,135   39,569     39,682</p>
<p>Gelman merger and restructuring charges</p>
<p>			     26,710	     -  30,621(b)	  -</p>
<p> Other charges	   43,360	     -   43,360	    -</p>
<p> Interest expense, net    629	   890    2,022	2,732</p>
<p>Total costs and expenses</p>
<p>			    315,749     220,862  744,914    628,236</p>
<p>(Loss)/earnings before</p>
<p>   income taxes	(40,410)	56,514   26,975    134,465</p>
<p> Income taxes	  (18,206)	15,916    2,927     40,251</p>
<p>Net (loss)/earnings</p>
<p>			(22,204)(c)	40,598  24,048(c)   94,214</p>
<p>Average number of shares</p>
<p>  outstanding	   126,684     125,373  126,027    124,973</p>
<p>(Loss)/earnings per share:</p>
<p>			  (0.18)(c)	  0.32  0.19(c)	 0.75</p>
<p>NOTE: Full company name is Pall Corp.  </p>
<p>(a) Includes inventory write-downs of $21,949.</p>
<p>In a written statement, the company said the third-quarter $0.18 per share loss reflected one-time charges (including the Gelman Sciences merger and restructuring charges) of $92.01 million, equal to $0.47 a share (after pro forma tax effect).  </p>
<p>(c) Excluding the Gelman merger and restructuring charges, other charges and inventory write-downs, net earnings and earnings per share for the quarter and nine months would have been $36,551,000 ($0.29 per share) and $86,433,000 ($0.69 per share), respectively.</p>
<p>In a written statement, the company said the $0.18 per share loss was due to one-time charges (including the Gelman Sciences merger and restructuring charges) of $92.01 million, equal to $0.47 a share (after pro forma tax effect).</p>
